{"kind":"request","text":"Each act declares the refusal names it can return.\n\nLet an act declare the closed set of refusal names it can produce, so a client or an agent knows every way the act can fail before it signs.\n\nSource: Hugh's request of 28 October 2026, after a review of the alchemy Domain package, where a command declares its rejections and the client's failure type is closed. The planner may attach this to an existing work item or sequence it.\n\nToday: `RefusalReason` in packages/contract/src/result.ts is one global union. A guard may declare a `reason` that the refusal carries as its `name`. An act does not say which reasons or names it can return, so a client must handle every member of the union, and an agent cannot tell a plausible refusal from an impossible one.\n\nWanted:\n1. An optional `refusals` list on an act type and on a handler: the guard reason names it can return. The validator refuses a declared guard reason that is not in the list and a listed name that no guard declares (`refusal-undeclared`, `refusal-unused`).\n2. The reasons that apply to every act (bad-intent, expired, revision-moved, scope-full and the like) stay implicit; the contract says which reasons are universal and which are act-specific.\n3. `declaredHandle` exposes an act's declared names in its types; the MCP tool description for an act lists them; the summary read publishes them so a client needs no definition in hand.\n4. The lending and counter definitions declare theirs. `dap check` reports an act whose guards declare no reason as a warning, not a refusal.\n\nThis adds an optional member to the definition format, so it falls under the kernel filing gate in docs/kernel.md section 7. The planner decides whether it is a format revision or an addition within `artroom-definition-1`.","body":{"conditions":"Landed on main with the format member, the validator rules, the typed handle and MCP exposure, and the lending and counter definitions updated; or superseded by a planner act naming the request that carries this work.","target_head":"0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}